NOTICE — attribution and upstream credits
==========================================

This repository is an independent reimplementation. The Rust code in
`minipro-rs/` and the analysis in `docs/` build on prior open-source
reverse-engineering of the XGecu T76 (and the T48/T56/TL866 family). That RE
established the *facts* this project implements — USB opcodes, packet layouts,
register/offset meanings, the T76's FPGA/bitstream operation sequence, and the
`InfoICT76.dll` field/variant transforms. Facts and interfaces are not
themselves copyrightable; the code here is original expression of them. The
work below is what made this possible and deserves full credit.

Matt Brown (nmatt0) — minipro `t76-improvements` fork
-----------------------------------------------------
    https://gitlab.com/nmatt0/minipro/-/tree/t76-improvements  (GPL-3.0)

The reverse-engineering of the T48/T56/T76 USB protocols, the T76's
FPGA/bitstream lifecycle, the firmware-update transport, and the `InfoICT76.dll`
field/variant transforms is Matt Brown's work. This project's drivers
(`minipro-rs/crates/minipro-proto/{t48,t56,t76}.rs`) and DLL parser
(`minipro-rs/crates/minipro-db/src/dll.rs`) are independent Rust
implementations of those reverse-engineered facts — not a translation of his
C source, which is not vendored in this repository.

radiomanV — Xgecu_T76 — FPGA-side tooling
-----------------------------------------
    https://github.com/radiomanV/Xgecu_T76  (The Unlicense)

